  const TALK = {
    m: [
      ['"I’m Odalys Brine. I teach the First Circle, where we start by using SQL to read the company books. The docks always need people who can do that, so pull up a chair if you’d like to learn."', '"Wex sent over more work from the quay, so pull up a chair. If there’s something in the example you’d like me to go through again, we have time."', '"When you bring me the result, keep the query with it. If Wex has a question later, you’ll be able to show him how you got it."', '"That’s the work I had for you here. If you want to keep learning, ask for Ilse Fenn in Brackwater. She’ll show you how to get the handful of rows you need from a full table."'],
      ['"Ilse Fenn. I look after accounts in the fens and teach the Second Circle. A boatman who needs three names has no use for a whole book, especially when the tide’s about to go out. I’ll show you how to find just the rows he can use."', '"Good to see you. I’ve got a list that needs going out, and the dispatch riders are already asking for it."', '"Read the request again before you run the query. I missed one of the conditions last week and had to run down the pier to get my notices back."', '"You’ve finished the files I set aside. Maud Tallow in Haverly will show you how to count what you find and compare it with the figures people bring you."'],
      ['"I’m Maud Tallow, and I run the counting room. If anybody brings me a total, I want to know what went into it. Take a seat and I’ll show you how we check those figures here."', '"You’re welcome to the chair if you move the ledgers off it. I have another report you can look at."', '"Leave your working where I can see it. I don’t enjoy guessing how other people got a number."', '"Take the river road to Four Fords if you want the next Circle. Tobin Ash can show you how to check two sets of records against each other. Tell him what you’re trying to find, or he’ll show you the whole dispatch book."'],
      ['"Tobin Ash. I teach the Fourth Circle, and the guild lets me use its dispatch books. The orders have numbers where the people unloading the carts need names. I’ll show you which columns let us bring the lists together."', '"Put your things down wherever there’s room. Someone sent me two reports that are supposed to describe the same goods. I could use another set of eyes."', '"When you join two lists, ask yourself what each row stands for. I once read two copies of the same dispatch as two deliveries. We sent the wagon out twice and paid the driver for both trips."', '"Brannoch Reeve is the person to ask about the next Circle. You’ll find him in Cinderwick. If he shows you a report that needs sorting out, ask him who it’s for. He likes to know you’re listening."'],
      ['"Brannoch Reeve. Mind the tray by the door. The people on my floor have to make decisions with the records we hand them. I teach the Fifth Circle so they get dates and labels they can actually use."', '"There’s a spare stool behind the bench. Bring it over. I can fit a lesson in before the afternoon shift comes through."', '"Before you hand me the sheet, picture somebody trying to read it while there’s a line at the counter."', '"That’s the last report I have for you. When you’re ready, go see Nym in Kell. She’ll show you how to use the answer to one query inside another."'],
      ['"Nym Sable. I look after the records here in Kell. When I need the answer to a small query to finish a bigger one, I can write both in the same statement. I teach that in the Sixth Circle."', '"Come closer to the lamp and tell me which report you’re working on. I’ll make room for it here."', '"If you get stuck, try running the smaller query on its own. It’s easier to fix when you can see what it returns."', '"Maren Holt teaches the next Circle in Highwatch. She’ll show you how to compare one row with the rest while keeping each row on the page."'],
      ['"I’m Maren Holt, and I teach the Seventh Circle here in Highwatch. I can show you how to compare a month’s sales with the months around it while keeping a row for each month. You’re welcome to catch your breath first. There’s a bench by the door."', '"Before you start on the report, tell me which rows you’ll compare. The next watch will need to know what you meant without coming to ask you."', '"Check the order of the rows you’re comparing. I had to ask for a new watch schedule once because I spent an afternoon working from the wrong end of one."', '"Ask for Bryn Okoro when you get to Aldermoot. He’ll give you a copy of the company books to practise on. I’ll be at the Audit when the council sits."'],
      ['"I’m Bryn Okoro, the Eighth Circle teacher. You’ll learn to add, change, and remove rows at the copy desks, where you can see what your query would do. Once a draft is checked, a clerk can use it to update the company books."', '"I have a clean copy ready. Show me which rows you plan to change before you work on them."', '"Someone has to be able to check your draft after you leave. Give them a clear way to see which rows you touched."', '"You’ve finished the exercises at my desk. Take the first seven marks to the hall if you’re ready for the Grand Audit. The council gives the eighth mark there."']
    ],
    s: [
      ['"I’m Pim Underhill. I study with Odalys and look after the stock sheets when she’s teaching. If you’ve got a little time, I have some work the two of us can go over."', '"Wex Carrow. I run the harbor. My crews have to read these sheets in the wind and rain, so I only send out what they need. Can you help me put a few together?"'],
      ['"Hob Sedge. I failed the Second Circle twice before Ilse gave me a desk here. If a filter keeps giving you the wrong rows, come look at the mistakes I kept making."', '"I’m Tam Osk. I look after the reed beds. I carry lists for the guild when I’m out checking the paths. Could you help me get them ready?"'],
      ['"Abbot Fenwright. I keep the chapel and its accounts. We buy some of our supplies from the guild, and they’ve sent me a copy of their stock list. Would you help me with the totals before I tell the parish what we can afford?"', '"Tessaly Roe. I keep sheep and help with the wool sales. I know who can do the work around here, and I need the figures before I can tell the town how many hands to hire."'],
      ['"Corwin Dale. Tobin’s been teaching me joins on the afternoon shift. I can show you the reports he gave me, if you don’t mind me looking at your answer."', '"Bly Hobb. I run the wagon yard. I’ve got people asking about bills and manifests every time I turn around. Can you help me match up the records?"'],
      ['"Ysolt Karn. I run the forge. If a buyer gives me a list of promises, I ask them when the goods actually arrived. I can show you how I read the two dates before I agree to another order."', '"Sefa Lund. I came here to learn the forge and ended up in the buying office. I’ll be glad to have company if you want to help with the reports."'],
      ['"Orrin Dusk. I cut stone for the guild. They offered me the orders to look over when I complained about how they packed it. Could you help me check a few?"', '"I’m Marrow Pike, from the deep chapel. Nym taught me enough to keep our books. There are a few company records I still need help to follow."'],
      ['"Calla Vane. I keep the tower logs. The guild sends me its order books to practise with. I use the same trick on both sets of records. I put the dates in order before I try to explain what changed."', '"Hale Verity. I handle guild accounts. Maren has been helping me read the work I’ve already done. I’m better at getting an order out the door than I am at looking back afterward."'],
      ['"Lune Farrow. I copy whatever the archivist brings me, and this week she’s let me build a practice table myself. You’re welcome to try it here."', '"Petra Voss, archivist. I keep the original records, and I make a copy when somebody needs to try a change. Let me show you what a clerk needs to see before they can use your draft."']
    ],
    praise: [
      ['"That’s the result Wex can use. Keep the query with it in case anyone needs to run it again."', '"That’s clear. I can use this to check the sheets I bring Odalys."', '"I can give that to the crew. Thanks for getting it ready."'],
      ['"That leaves me exactly the people I came looking for. I’ll get a copy out to the riders."', '"I can see why those rows stayed in. I wish I’d worked it out that quickly at my first examination."', '"Thank you. Now I can get this into the right hands without making another trip."'],
      ['"That accounts for what’s in the book. Leave me the figures, please."', '"I can bring those numbers to the chapel. Thank you for taking the time to check them."', '"That’s what I needed. I can make a decision with that."'],
      ['"That agrees with both books. Leave a copy by the dispatch window, would you?"', '"I see how you matched the rows. I’m going to try it that way myself."', '"I can use that in the wagon yard. You’ve saved me a trip to the quay."'],
      ['"Good. The person at the bench will know what to do with this."', '"That’s ready to use. Thanks for putting it in a form I can work with."', '"That came out the way Brannoch asked. I’ll have a copy ready for him when he gets in."'],
      ['"That answers the question. I’ll keep a copy here while I check the records that go with it."', '"Thanks. I can follow the steps you took to get there."', '"I can show that to the chapel board. It helps that I can tell them where the totals came from."'],
      ['"That’s what I asked for. Keep the order of those rows in mind when you do the next report."', '"That reads cleanly. I’ll put it with the other reports for the next shift."', '"Thanks for taking a look. I can work with that result."'],
      ['"That does what the request calls for. I’d show that copy to a clerk."', '"I can show Petra how you got that result. She’ll ask, so I’ll keep your query with the copy."', '"I’ve checked your result. I’ll keep it with the query so the next clerk can see how we got it."']
    ],
    rival: [
      '"I’m Dregan Vosk, out of Ironwake. I told the others Tallyport wouldn’t have the nerve to send anyone after Corin died. If you fancy a duel, I’ll give you a chance to make me take that back."',
      '"People here call me Sister Calloway. I’m carrying the Reedbinder Order’s colors. I have a few minutes before I have to get back to the sick house. Would you like a bout?"',
      '"Pell Marrow. I’ve entered four times and my daughter says I’m still making the same mistakes. Maybe you can show me which ones."',
      '"Jessamy Crane, Longroad. I keep an eye on who’s coming through. If you’ve got time to set your bag down, I’ve got a wager in mind."',
      '"Call me Ilgrave. The smiths can argue about which fighter has the best chance until the forge goes cold. I’d rather have a bout and find out something for myself."',
      '"I go by the Archivist Under. I’d like a match, and that’s all you need to know about me until it’s over."',
      '"Lady Oriel Vant. I’ve trained on this mountain since I could walk, and I’m tired of hearing what a surprise the next candidate will be. Let’s see you duel."',
      '"I’m Hale Quarto, from the Chancery. I spent all morning copying papers for the council. Would you do me the favor of a bout? I’d like to spend half an hour on something I chose myself."'
    ],
    again: ['"I left the next job on the desk if you want it."', '"Thanks for coming back. I’ve got another file open."', '"I can show you the next one whenever you’re ready."'],
    place: ['"The docks keep us busy even when the weather closes the harbor. If you come back late, the tavern keeps a light in the front window."', '"The streets run over the water here. Stay on the boards in town. The reed cutters use the paths out beyond the houses."', '"Most people here make a living off the flocks or the counting rooms. The hawks nest high on the slopes outside town."', '"The wagons bring wool and food through here. If you walk out past the fields, give the wolves and the road bandits room."', '"The forge runs all day. Keep clear of the vents and the spiders that nest around them."', '"People bring their own lamps down from the road and find we hardly need them in town. Past the houses, the caves drop into dark passages."', '"The watch looks out from the tower every night it can see the water. Bring something warm if you head into the crags."', '"The council sits above the city and the old record rooms are underneath. The clerks have been carrying files up since dawn."'],
    tav: ['"The table by the stove is free. Leave your boots on the mat if you’ve come straight from the pier."', '"You can sit by the railing if you like. Mind the step, the water’s high."', '"The mutton’s ready. If you’d rather wait for the pie, I can bring you something to drink."', '"Put your pack under the bench. Two wagon crews are due in and they never look where they put their feet."', '"If you’ve come from the forge, I’ve got water to help you cool down. There’s room upstairs if you want a quieter table."', '"There’s a quiet table upstairs if you want it. The people on this floor are coming off shift and I won’t be asking them to whisper."', '"Come off the step and shut the door. I’ve got hot soup for whoever finds a seat."', '"You can read at the table. I just ask that you leave the inkpot on the tray."'],
    heal: ['"Sit down. I’ll see what needs binding."', '"Put your hand there and hold the cloth in place while I get a fresh one."', '"Come in. There’s another bench if you need to lie down."'],
    stall: ['"Take a look. I can show you anything you’re thinking of buying."', '"The gear I brought in this morning is on the table. I can take used things in trade for coin."', '"I buy as well as sell. Let me know what you came for."'],
    way: ['"Come over by the fire. I’ve got a few things for the road if you’re running short."', '"I bring food out for the people who work up here. If you’re going farther, I can sell you something to eat or a healing draught."', '"I can sell you a draught if you’ve used yours up, or a ration if what you need is a meal."'],
    bark: ['"I’m waiting for my brother to get off shift. If you see him carrying a shovel, tell him I brought supper."', '"I thought I’d have this lamp fixed by the time it got dark. I’d better find a match."', '"If you see a goat by the road, tell the baker. She’s been looking for hers since breakfast."', '"My cousin took the Trials. He works in the counting house now, and he says he finally has time to bring the children home for supper."', '"I wrote my first query yesterday. It took me half an hour and I asked the baker to come look at it."', '"We had rain up here all morning. I hope the road was dry where you came from."', '"The guildhall’s been busy. I’m going to leave it until the next shift to pick up my papers."'],
    hint: ['"There are campfires out along the longer roads. You can rest at one when you reach it."', '"Old chests turn up in the wilds, away from the roads. Try walking off the road if you have time to look."', '"Each Circle master sells common pages for that Circle. You have to find the rare ones out in the world."', '"If your First Circle strike barely scratches a creature, try a page from a higher Circle. A correct query gives full power for that page, but your weapon skill still determines your chance to hit."', '"If you fall, the healer can bring you back. You’ll have ten minutes to get your belongings. If you fell in a dungeon, look by the entrance on the surface."', '"Open your map and look for named hunting grounds. It’s easier to avoid trouble if you can see where the creatures are."', '"Meat and other food can heal you. Open your bag and pick something to eat."', '"Ask in the guildhall where to find the Examiner’s ring. Someone can tell you which road to take."', '"A woman left journal pages along the road this spring. Look beside the old signposts away from the main path."', '"The bank can hold spare gold and gear. You can go back for it after a fight."'],
    marked: ['"I’ve seen that kind of mark on people passing through. You must’ve put some work in to get it."', '"My daughter saw an Examiner’s mark for the first time this morning. She’s been asking how to earn one ever since."'],
  };

